Done. Nothing committed.

**What I found (critique):** the branch's latest "deliverable" commit only touched log files — the rework the owner required in issue comments (email-protected owner account, URL-based mounting replacing the in-app toggle, checkbox permission UI) was entirely unimplemented, despite the plan flagging it. Also confirmed the known double-`<ChatWindow/>` bug.

**Fixes/hardening delivered:**
- `src/server/routes/admin.ts`: `PROTECTED_OWNER_EMAIL` constant + 400 on demoting `formsatz@gmail.com`, layered before the last-admin count check.
- `src/client/src/App.tsx`: `/admin` URL mounting via `isAdminRoute()`, toggle removed, duplicate ChatWindow removed, `Back to chat` link.
- `src/client/src/components/AdminView.tsx`: permission checkboxes writing the full array via PUT.
- New tests: 2 server (owner demotion blocked even with 2nd admin; 2nd-admin demotion still allowed), 2 client (checkbox on/off paths), 3 client App tests (`/admin` mounting for admins, silent chat fallback for non-admins, admin link href).
- Verified `vite preview` serves `/admin` with 200 + app HTML — no compose/vite config change needed.

**Verification:** `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, server tests (37 passed), client lint/tests (12 passed), `npm run format:check`, and `npm run ci` — all green.

**Docs/comms:** plan doc steps now honestly marked done with findings recorded; two new open questions (non-admin `/admin` fallback UX; admin view styling) added under 'Open questions' and posted to #15: https://github.com/alex-moon/tova/issues/15#issuecomment-5632082308
